cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "INTERCEPTA: a reproducible cell-line/ex-vivo transcriptomic drug-response + mechanism engine"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Akula
    given-names: Prasad
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-29
url: "https://github.com/AKULA-PRASAD/intercepta-build"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A reproducible, pre-registered, integrity-first engine for transcriptomic cancer drug-response prediction.
  Establishes a leakage-free cross-dataset cell-line transfer ceiling (rho=+0.212), genome-wide AML mutation-drug
  markers, a weak drug-specific ex-vivo signal, OOD-calibrated confidence, and — as a first-class negative result —
  a well-powered NULL for human clinical drug-response prediction driven by cancer-type confounding. Honestly
  scoped: a research/hypothesis-ranking engine, NOT a validated clinical predictor.
keywords:
  - drug response prediction
  - pharmacogenomics
  - reproducibility
  - cancer
